/-!
# The generic point of a geometrically irreducible fibre

Let `R → B` be a smooth ring map such that the fibres of `Spec B → Spec R` are geometrically
irreducible, and let `r` be a prime of `R`. Then the ideal `rB` is again prime: it is the generic
point of the fibre of `Spec B → Spec R` over `r`.

The fibre over the *generic* point of `Spec(R/r)` is integral, by smoothness and geometric
irreducibility, and `Spec(B/rB) → Spec(R/r)` is a smooth — hence flat and open — morphism onto
the irreducible reduced scheme `Spec(R/r)`. Flatness forces every generic point of `Spec(B/rB)`
into the fibre over the generic point of `Spec(R/r)`, so `Spec(B/rB)` is irreducible, and
geometric reducedness over a reduced base makes it reduced. An integral affine scheme is the
spectrum of a domain, so `rB` is prime.

## Main results

* `Ideal.isPrime_map_of_smooth_of_geometricallyIrreducible`: for a smooth algebra whose spectrum
  has geometrically irreducible fibres, the extension of a prime of the base is prime.

## Implementation notes

The statement is the one that makes condition (7) of Stacks 05HX — that `α` becomes an
isomorphism over the residue field of `rB` — expressible at all, and it is the field
`Module.CompleteDevissage.map_isPrime`.

It generalises `Algebra.closedFiberIdeal_isPrime`, which is the special case of a local base ring
and its maximal ideal, from geometrically *integral* fibres to the weaker hypotheses of a
complete dévissage: smoothness plus geometrically irreducible fibres. The local case can read off
integrality of the closed fibre directly from the hypothesis, whereas for a general prime the
fibre over `r` is the fibre over a point that is not closed, so integrality of `B ⊗ R/r` has to be
assembled out of irreducibility and reducedness separately.

Irreducibility comes from `AlgebraicGeometry.GeometricallyIrreducible.irreducibleSpace`, which
needs the morphism to be open; a smooth morphism is. Reducedness comes from
`AlgebraicGeometry.GeometricallyReduced.isReduced_of_flat_of_finite_irreducibleComponents`, whose
finiteness hypothesis on the irreducible components of the base is satisfied because `Spec(R/r)`
is irreducible and therefore has exactly one.

Both the base ring and the algebra live in the same universe, since the proof passes through
their spectra.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 05HX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05HX)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 056T](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/056T)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits
open scoped TensorProduct

universe u

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 05HX.** If `R → B` is smooth and the fibres of `Spec B → Spec R` are
geometrically irreducible, then the ideal generated by a prime `r` of `R` in `B` is prime. It is
the generic point of the fibre over `r`. -/
@[stacks 05HX "the prime of the lower algebra"]
theorem Ideal.isPrime_map_of_smooth_of_geometricallyIrreducible
    (R B : Type u) [CommRing R] [CommRing B] [Algebra R B] [Algebra.Smooth R B]
    [GeometricallyIrreducible (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap R B)))]
    (r : Ideal R) [r.IsPrime] : (Ideal.map (algebraMap R B) r).IsPrime := by
  set f : Spec (.of B) ⟶ Spec (.of R) := Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap R B)) with hf
  set g : Spec (.of (R ⧸ r)) ⟶ Spec (.of R) :=
    Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap R (R ⧸ r))) with hg
  have hfsm : Smooth f := by
    rw [hf]
    exact (HasRingHomProperty.Spec_iff (P := @Smooth)).2
      (RingHom.smooth_algebraMap.2 inferInstance)
  have hsm : Smooth (pullback.snd f g) := inferInstance
  have hfin : Finite (irreducibleComponents (Spec (CommRingCat.of (R ⧸ r)))) := by
    rw [irreducibleComponents_eq_singleton]; infer_instance
  have hgr : GeometricallyReduced (pullback.snd f g) :=
    geometricallyReduced_of_smooth (pullback.snd f g)
  have hX : IsReduced (pullback f g) :=
    GeometricallyReduced.isReduced_of_flat_of_finite_irreducibleComponents (pullback.snd f g)
  have hXirr := GeometricallyIrreducible.irreducibleSpace (pullback.snd f g)
    (Scheme.Hom.isOpenMap (pullback.snd f g))
  set e := pullbackSpecIso R B (R ⧸ r) with he
  have hred : IsReduced (Spec (CommRingCat.of (B ⊗[R] (R ⧸ r)))) :=
    isReduced_of_isOpenImmersion e.inv
  have hirr : IrreducibleSpace (Spec (CommRingCat.of (B ⊗[R] (R ⧸ r)))) :=
    (TopCat.homeoOfIso (Scheme.forgetToTop.mapIso e)).irreducibleSpace_iff.mp hXirr
  have hD : IsDomain (B ⊗[R] (R ⧸ r)) :=
    (affine_isIntegral_iff (CommRingCat.of (B ⊗[R] (R ⧸ r)))).mp
      (isIntegral_of_irreducibleSpace_of_isReduced _)
  exact (Ideal.Quotient.isDomain_iff_prime _).mp
    (MulEquiv.isDomain _ (Algebra.TensorProduct.quotIdealMapEquivTensorQuot B r).toMulEquiv)

end
